course: dictionary
lesson: 4786
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word hum has more than one meaning, so the words around it show you which one fits. «The fridge hummed all night in the kitchen.» Fridges make noise, not songs, so hummed means a low, steady buzzing sound.
explain: «When you hum, your vocal cords wobble as air from your lungs passes them, and you can feel the buzz on your throat.» Here hum is a sound you make yourself, singing a tune with your lips closed. The clue is that you can feel the buzz.
explain: Hum can also be a noun, meaning the low, continuous sound itself: «the hum of traffic». To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. Does «the buzz of traffic» still make sense? If it does, your meaning fits.
fact: Hum means to sing a tune with your lips closed, making a long «mmm» sound.
fact: Hum also means to make a low, steady buzzing sound, like bees or a fridge.
fact: As a noun, a hum is a low, continuous sound: «the hum of traffic».
fact: «Humming with activity» means busy and lively, as in «The classroom was humming with activity».
fact: «Noise-cancelling headphones work best on a low, steady hum, like a train or a plane engine.» A steady hum is a sound that stays the same for a long time.
exercise: «The fridge hummed all night.» What does hummed mean here? | *To make a low, steady buzzing sound | To sing a happy tune | To shout loudly | To be busy and lively
exercise: Ella says, «I can hum my favourite tune with my lips closed.» What is she doing? | Shouting for help | *Singing with her lips closed, making a long «mmm» sound | Chewing her lunch | Whistling through her teeth
exercise: «The hum of traffic filled the street.» What is a hum in this sentence? | A quick, sharp shout | *A low, continuous sound | A type of bread | A bright light
test: «The classroom was humming with activity.» What does humming mean here? | Still and silent | Making a low buzzing sound | Singing quietly | *Busy and lively
test: Which sentence uses hum as a noun? | «The bees hum in the garden.» | «We hum a tune before we sing.» | «Mum hummed in the kitchen.» | *«The hum of the engine filled the room.»
exam: «Noise-cancelling headphones work best on a low, steady hum, like a train or a plane engine.» What does hum mean in this sentence? | To be very busy | To sing a tune | A loud crash | *A low, steady sound
